%U A239300 12832537722358410,282336283791432866,6324511917177082209
%N A239300 Words of length n over the alphabet {0,...,n-1} that are 1324-avoiding.
%C A239300 A word w contains 1324 if there are positions i < j < k < l with w(i) < w(k) < w(j) < w(l). Writing p(j) for the minimum letter before position j, w contains 1324 if and only if there are positions j < k < l with p(j) < w(k) < w(j) < w(l). This gives a left-to-right transfer-matrix computation whose state records only the least letter so far, the least w(j) over completed 132-occurrences, and, for each value x, the least w(j) with p(j) < x < w(j); the number of reachable states is small (18550573 at n = 16), so a(n) is obtainable far beyond brute force. - _Stephen J. Pursey_, Sep 07 2026
%o A239300 (Python)
%o A239300 from itertools import product, combinations
%o A239300 def avoids(w):
%o A239300     return not any(w[i] < w[k] < w[j] < w[l] for i, j, k, l in combinations(range(len(w)), 4))
%o A239300 def a(n): return sum(avoids(w) for w in product(range(n), repeat=n))
%o A239300 print([a(n) for n in range(8)]) # _Stephen J. Pursey_, Sep 07 2026
%Y A239300 The permutation analog is A061552.
%Y A239300 Cf. A000312.
